  "mathematical_findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Original row domains and ordered access",
      "finding": "Shared interface is byte-identical to the reviewed pilot: row Fin144, ordered vertex Fin9 and coordinate Fin8. rawVertices follows concreteGeometry01.rows[r].vertexIds[i] -> concreteGeometry01.vertices[id][j]. Geometry and moment records use the same original ordinal; no sorting, subset guard or reindexing of vertex order is introduced."
    },
    {
      "topic": "No fallback",
      "finding": "The unchanged interface exposes no-fallback equalities for raw geometry row, moment row, vertex/coordinate lookup, factor maxima, weighted means and Q80 factor integers. They use existing bounded-access and shape theorems at the actual finite index. Every remaining finite supplier raw_row_eq/raw_vertices_eq/raw_moment_row_eq signature was checked at its own exact ordinal."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Original rationalMoment",
      "finding": "rawOriginalMoments explicitly calls P2OriginalSaving19HigherMoments.rationalMoment with original gapQ vertices and deviations 1 - factorsQ(vertex,j)/factorMaxima[j]. Its equality to the generic originalMoments is rfl. Generic source remains exact accepted-coordinator SHA 9f4b64321975f8eb567484982abc622ee77ac222c90a6d117b2acc7a0f39b574; no different moment formula is substituted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Five original floor clauses",
      "finding": "OriginalFloorChecksFor retains mean/first-moment equality, ten saved factor floor equalities in the original checker namespace, old-floor/geometry Jensen equality, old-floor/original-operator equality and saved-new = max(original old operator, uncapped original new operator). No clause or max argument is removed."
